          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How can I find a stud without any finder?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Look for clues first: outlets and switches usually sit beside a stud, baseboard and trim nails line up with framing, and studs repeat every 16 inches from a corner. Knock and listen for a duller sound. Then drive a thin finish nail in a spot that will be hidden. Solid resistance after the drywall means wood."
