        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          The cheap stud finder that came free with a toolkit is why so many people think stud finders do not work. The single-pad capacitive design needs a perfect calibration on a blank patch of wall and still guesses at the edges. Multi-sensor arrays fixed most of that a few years ago by showing the whole stud at once, and a two-dollar magnet still beats every electronic tool on old lath and plaster. Pick by wall type first, features second.
